      "handoff_review": "Existing canonical source responsibilities are associated under the accepted product purpose. Four broad requirements remain unbound: portable-validation, external-normalization, schema-compatibility and cli-and-fixtures. The linked tests establish only the four named local fixture scopes. They do not establish all-model negative coverage, arbitrary raw-field preservation, reverse-adapter correctness, exhaustive compatibility evolution, cross-language validation, installed package parity or real downstream adoption. Example/CI/release/support paths participate as ownership/freshness support, not independent behavior proof. docs/stability.md is the direct compatibility owner; contradictory adapter-guide wording was corrected to that existing policy after review. External harnesses own evaluation execution and result correctness.",
